{title: Father to the Fatherless}
{subtitle: Psalms 68:6}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 78}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Am/C] | [Bb] |
| [F] [Am7/E] | [Dm] | [Am/C] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
As smoke is [Dm]driven a[Am/C]way
The wicked [Bb]perish in the [F]fire
But let the [Dm]righteous be [Am/C]glad
Exulting be[Bb]fore Him [Dm]higher
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
A [Bb]father to the [C]father[Dm]less
A de[Bb]fender [C]of wid[Dm]ows
[Bb]God in his [C]holy d[Dm]welling
Singing [Bb]praises [C]to his [Dm]name
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Lift up a song for the [Am/C]Lord
Who [Bb]rides through the de[F]serts
Rejoice be[Dm]fore him al[Am/C]ways
His [Bb]name [C]is the [Dm]Lord
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Bb]Settles the [C]lonely in a [Dm]home
Leads [Bb]prisoners to [C]prosper[Dm]ity
The re[Bb]bellious [C]dwell in [Dm]scorched land
[Bb]Earth shook and [C]heavens poured [Dm]rain
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The One of [Bb]Sinai
[C]God of [Dm]Is[Am/C]rael [Bb][Dm]
{end_of_verse}
